<title>GERMANY: Allianz details corporate shareholdings.</title>
<headline>Allianz details corporate shareholdings.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>German insurance group Allianz AG Holding on Monday revealed for the first time its shareholdings below five percent in German and foreign companies, with a total market value of 3.744 billion marks.</p>
<p>At its annual shareholder meeting the group said it held three percent of German utility group Viag AG, three percent of Siemens, two percent of Daimler-Benz and 0.8 percent of machinery group Mannesmann AG.</p>
<p>It also owns 2.6 percent of Bavaria's Bayerische Vereinsbank and four percent of metals group Metallgesellshaft AG.</p>
<p>Among foreign companies, Allianz said it owned 3.4 percent of Banco Popular of Spain, three percent of Italy's Credito Italiano, 3.2 percent of Credito Romagnolo and three percent of Istituto Mobiliare Italiano (IMI).</p>
<p>The group also owns many other shareholdings above five percent, which are already known. These include stakes in utilities Veba AG and RWE and Deutsche Bank AG and Dresdner Bank AG.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
